  "summary_text": "Kyle, yesterday was softer than it should have been, but the year-to-date momentum is real and the structural drivers are in your favor.\n\nPort Washington had a rough Friday\u2014down 40% in total revenue and 46% in transactions versus the prior Friday. However, this was a capacity story, not a performance story. You ran 4 groomers at $424 per groomer, 10% below your trailing 30-day baseline of $474. The team executed fine; you simply had fewer hands on the floor. The good news: month-to-date Port Washington is +11% absolute and +4% after adjusting for calendar mix. Year-to-date you're up 45% in revenue and 44% in appointments\u2014that's the real signal. Hicksville is even hotter on the calendar: +25% MTD absolute and +17.4% after DOW-adjustment, despite being down 34% yesterday. Retail at Hicksville tanked 67% yesterday, which is worth watching for front-of-house focus, but the grooming attach rate is solid at 46%, so upsell discipline is holding.\n\nOne concern: Hicksville has no bathers scheduled for the next 7 days and tomorrow drops to zero groomers. That's a structural gap that will suppress productivity. Port Washington's lapse pool sits at $296k in annual value\u2014469 dormant or drifting customers\u2014while Hicksville's is $91k across 119 customers. Both are reactivation opportunities, but Port Washington's is the bigger lever.\n\n**Capacity & coverage:** Today you have 7 active groomer-days (4 Port Washington, 3 Hicksville) plus 8.0 bather hours at Port Washington; tomorrow drops to 1 groomer and 7.0 bather hours; next 7 days: 56 groomer-days total (38 Port Washington, 18 Hicksville) with only Port Washington running bather support (43 hours, zero at Hicksville)."
